Improved: With device-aware MPI, Utilities::MPI::Partitioner now packs the
data for all import targets in export_to_ghosted_array_start(), and applies
the data from all import targets in import_from_ghosted_array_finish(), with
a single kernel and a single fence instead of one kernel and one fence per
target. The imported data is applied in the same order as before, so the
results do not change. This reduces the latency of
LinearAlgebra::distributed::Vector::update_ghost_values() and compress() for
vectors in MemorySpace::Default.
<br>
(Shubham Goswami, 2026/10/26)
